7. THE INTENT THE PATCHED BOARD P GENERATOR WRITES FOR THE NEW NETS
   rail PACK_P   source W_P, loads {"Q101": 5.0, "Q102": 5.0}, switch U101 on BRK_UVLO
   rail BRK_VIN  source Q2, loads {"R101": 6.52, "R102": 3.48}, switch U1 on DSG_R, series of PACK_P
   rail BRK_SNS  source ['R101', 'R102'], loads {"Q101": 5.0, "Q102": 5.0}, switch - on -, series of PACK_P
   rail VCC_F    source R7, loads {"U1": 0.00034}, switch U1 on DSG_R, fed from BRK_VIN
   node BRK_GATE    v_max 29.4 V, rides on PACK_P by 12.6 V
   node BRK_UVLO    v_max 29.2 V
   node BRK_G2      v_max 14.6 V
   node BRK_CMID    v_max 29.2 V
   node DOCK_EN_OUT v_max 29.2 V
   node DOCK_EN_RET v_max 17.4 V
   clamp D101: uni, protected BRK_VIN, return PACK_N

8. FINDINGS FOR OTHER AUTHORS (run-time refusals of the composed generators that no text-level composition test reads)
   L8P-F01 board E: l4e7's backstop draft: C66, C67 and C68 carry no G14 decoupling class
   L8P-F03 board E: l4e11's aux draft: +12V_FAN names L4 as its source, which is not on that net
   L8P-F02 board A: l4e11's charger draft: VSYS_DOCK names U42 as its source without source_ic, and is fed from VBAT before VBAT is declared

